Subject: [PATCH] ua: drop the Headless token from the User-Agent

With --headless, stock Chromium writes HeadlessChrome into the
User-Agent. No regular Chrome sends that token, so a server or page can
spot automation from it alone. The product token stays Chrome in
headless mode, and every header and JavaScript value built from the
User-Agent follows.

diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
index 3f87ec8..53e9d4d 100644
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
@@ -215,9 +215,12 @@ const blink::UserAgentBrandList GetUserAgentBrandFullVersionListInternal(
 // depending on the Reduce User-Agent reduction phase features.
 std::string GetUserAgentInternal() {
   std::string product = GetProductAndVersion();
-  if (base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(kHeadless)) {
-    product.insert(0, "Headless");
-  }
+  // Apostate: upstream prefixes the product token with "Headless" whenever the
+  // --headless switch is present. That token describes how this browser was
+  // launched, not the device it represents, and no real Chrome ever sends it.
+  // It is inserted here, upstream of the User-Agent string and of every header
+  // and JavaScript value derived from it, so removing it at this point is
+  // sufficient and there is no second path to cover.
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
   if (base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(kUseMobileUserAgent)) {
